Z||000000||Ironhorse||04-30-2000||07:47 PM||||Hello... I have a 1985 Fiero 2.8 liter engine that threw a rod... I'm going to install a 1987 Fiero 2.8 engine.  I come to find out that the Timing chain cover is not the same on 85 2.8 and 87 2.8.  How come they are different? Can I take 85 timing chain cover, waterpump, harmonic balancer, and pulley onto a 87 2.8 without a problem... Please help, it's GONNA BE A F**KIN' HELL to find a timing chain cover for 87 2.8 since they discontinue it and only makes them for Fiero.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Frank R||05-01-2000||01:22 AM||||Easy big guy.  There are lots of parts out there for you.  Usually each time there is a change in any product, it is for the betterment of that product.  This maybe a good change for your car.  Begin to make some phone calls and discover what the change maybe and how it will affect the engine.  Call Napa or any other with high dollar parts.  They will know any mechanical upgrade.  All engine machine shops know any changes between same engine of different years.  Gather info......Then you may panic.<BR>Frank R...||||reg||6
Z||000002||Ironhorse||05-01-2000||06:00 PM||||Hey FrankR.. heh I've tried that... I contacted Napa, Autozone, GM, Pontiac dealer, and etc... they all become humble and dumb when I mention the word Fiero... that's all it takes, they would have PHD degree in cars and etc, and when I say the word Fiero their money for education to get a PHD goes down the toilet.  I didn't panic early mind you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> If anyone have more information or place to contact please inform me... Thanks.. BTW sorry for my poor choice of words eariler||||reg||1
